### Phase 2 — Scan: delete the ink program, realign the tests

The digital-ink handwriting recognizer is being removed permanently. Production
Scan is camera + printed-text OCR; the ink code was a separate architecture that
nothing in `lib/` ever used. Verified before deleting: `ink_stroke.dart` was
imported only by `ink_canvas.dart` and three test files, and `ink_canvas.dart`
by two more. Only `test/ink_lines_test.dart` was ever git-tracked.

Simplify the multi-candidate machinery at the same time. `RecognizedLine` once
held every reading ML Kit offered so the matcher could pick the best, but
`MlKitTextRecognizer` has only ever returned one candidate per line, so the whole
multi-candidate path — `candidates`, `best`, the readings loop in `_rank`, the
strongest-reading tie-break, `PrescriptionSuggestion.reading`, and
`ScanScreen._displayFor` — was unreachable. The fuzzy-scoring core
(`_similarity`, `_ratio`, `_editDistance`, `_contains`, `_coverage`,
`_normalise`, `_tokens` and the thresholds) is kept exactly as it was.

